  "title": "Cream cheese Bundt cake",
  "subtitle": "dense, tender lemon-scented Bundt cake with a cream cheese crumb",
  "excerpt": "Cream cheese folded into the batter of a Bundt cake adds richness and a subtle tang that enriches a standard sponge without making it heavy. The cake has a very fine, velvety crumb and bakes to a deep golden crust from the Bundt tin's surface area. It needs no frosting: a dusting of icing sugar over the warm cake is the traditional finish, though a thin lemon glacé icing poured over the inverted cake is an easy addition.",
