  "sourceNotes": "The Bundt tin (a ring mould with a fluted outer surface) was popularised in the United States by Nordic Ware from 1950, though fluted ring cake tins have a Central European (German and Austrian) heritage. The cream-cheese-enriched cake batter became a standard American home baking format from the 1970s onward, documented in Pillsbury bakeoff collections and other American recipe publications of the period.",
