  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A Bundt cake's intricate surface requires a tin that is properly prepared: butter every groove of the tin, dust with flour, and tap out the excess. Any bare patch will cause the cake to stick and tear when inverted. Some bakers use a baking spray with flour incorporated; the outcome is the same. Take the butter and cream cheese out of the fridge 1 hour before you start; both must be at room temperature or the batter will be lumpy."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
