      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cream the butter and cheese"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Heat the oven to 170°C (conventional). Generously butter every groove and surface of a 24 cm Bundt tin, then dust with flour and tap out the excess. Beat {{unsalted-butter}}, {{cream-cheese}}, and {{caster-sugar}} together in a stand mixer on medium speed for 4 minutes until very pale, light, and fluffy. Add the zest of {{lemon}} and {{vanilla-extract}}."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Add the eggs and fold in the flour"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Add {{eggs}} one at a time, beating well after each addition. Reduce the speed to low. Sift {{plain-flour}}, {{baking-powder}}, and {{sea-salt-fine}} over the mixture and fold in by hand with a spatula until just combined. Do not beat once the flour goes in."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bake and unmould"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Spoon the batter into the prepared tin and smooth the top. Bake for 55 to 60 minutes until the top is golden and a skewer inserted into the thickest part comes out clean. Leave in the tin for 20 minutes on a wire rack. Invert the tin confidently onto the rack, leave for 1 minute, then lift the tin straight up. Dust with {{icing-sugar}} while still warm. Serve warm or at room temperature."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
